            DateTimeFormatter formatter = DateTimeFormatter.ofPattern("MMM dd, yyyy HH:mm", Locale.ENGLISH);

            BlogPost p0 = new BlogPost();
            p0.setTitle("How to Use QR Codes in Real Estate to Reach More Buyers");
            p0.setExcerpt("Real estate marketing runs on mobile, and QR Codes give agents a contactless bridge between physical marketing materials and mobile digital experiences.");
            p0.setAuthor("Admin");
            p0.setCategory("Professional Services, QR Codes");
            p0.setReadTime("11 min read");
            p0.setImageUrl(qrBase64);
            p0.setContent("[{\"heading\":\"\",\"body\":[\"Real estate marketing runs on mobile, and QR Codes give agents a contactless bridge between physical marketing materials and mobile digital experiences. Prospective buyers can scan a code to open property details, schedule a viewing, or explore a virtual tour right from their smartphones. It’s a fast, frictionless way to move someone from a curbside sign to a full listing on their smartphone in a single tap.\",\"That mobile-first habit is already the norm. The National Association of Realtors found that 69% of buyers use a mobile or tablet device in their home search, and 51% found the last home they purchased online. Meeting buyers on the devices they already use turns everyday marketing pieces into interactive touchpoints. When a sign or flyer opens directly to a mobile listing, you shorten the path from first glance to a booked showing.\"]},{\"heading\":\"Key takeaways\",\"body\":[\"Use Dynamic QR Codes so you can update a listing’s destination anytime without reprinting signs or flyers.\",\"Track every scan with Bitly Analytics to see which listings, locations, and materials drive the most buyer interest.\",\"Brand every QR Code with your logo and colors, since branded codes earn more scans and signal a trustworthy agent.\",\"Pair each code with a clear call to action, such as 'Scan to book a tour,' to convert curiosity into booked showings.\",\"Link codes to mobile-friendly Bitly Pages so buyers reach property details in a single tap.\"]},{\"heading\":\"Why realtors are turning to QR Codes for modern marketing\",\"body\":[\"QR Codes work because they extend a digital habit agents already have, but if you are new to the format, our guide to how QR Codes work covers the basics. The National Association of Realtors reports that 75% of members use social media and 52% use drone photography or video in their work, so adding a scannable code to physical materials is a natural next step if you’re not already doing so. It connects the online tools you rely on to the signs, flyers, and mailers buyers encounter in the real world.\"]},{\"heading\":\"QR Codes meet clients where they are: On mobile\",\"body\":[\"QR Codes let buyers reach property information instantly, without typing a URL or running a complicated search. A code on a for-sale sign, business card, or postcard can open listing details, contact info, or a virtual tour in seconds. QR Codes for real estate agents meet the moment when a buyer is most curious, whether they’re standing at the curb or flipping through a mailer at home, and keep them moving toward a showing.\"]},{\"heading\":\"They’re easy to create, edit, and reuse\",\"body\":[\"Dynamic QR Codes let you change the destination URL after you print or share a code, unlike static codes that lock in one link forever. When a price drops or a viewing schedule shifts, you can update each code’s destination in a few clicks instead of reprinting materials.\",\"One code can carry a listing from first showing to closing day, and the same code can then move on to your next property. That flexibility saves both money and time, which matters when you juggle several active listings at once. QR Codes are among the top tools for real estate agents, and it’s easy to integrate Dynamic QR Codes into your marketing.\"]},{\"heading\":\"They make marketing measurable\",\"body\":[\"QR Codes turn offline marketing into data you can act on. Bitly Analytics tracks code scan activity in real time, including total scans and breakdowns by city, country, and device type. You can see which listings, locations, and materials generate the most buyer interest, then shift your budget and placement toward what works. That same data helps you show sellers a clear record of how their listing performed, building trust and winning repeat business.\"]},{\"heading\":\"Static vs. Dynamic QR Codes: which realtors should use\",\"table\":{\"headers\":[\"Feature\",\"Static QR Code\",\"Dynamic QR Code\"],\"rows\":[[\"Editable after printing\",\"No\",\"Yes\"],[\"Scan tracking and analytics\",\"No\",\"Yes\"],[\"Best for\",\"Fixed info like a permanent contact link\",\"Listings, open houses, and anything that changes\"]]},\"body\":[\"Static QR Codes are fixed the moment you generate them, while Dynamic QR Codes use a short, editable redirect URL that lets you change their destination without reprinting (and unlock automated scan tracking). The difference matters most when your content changes often, which is true for almost every real estate listing.\",\"For real estate, where listings move quickly from active to pending to sold, Dynamic QR Codes are the better default.\"]},{\"heading\":\"Examples of how to use QR Codes to promote real estate listings\",\"body\":[\"QR Codes fit almost every place you already market a listing, from the yard sign out front to the mailer in a buyer’s hands. Here are five practical placements and how to make each one work harder:\"]},{\"heading\":\"On for-sale signs and window displays\",\"body\":[\"A QR Code on a real estate sign or storefront lets passersby pull up listing details, contact information, or a virtual tour at any hour, even after your office closes. Reusable sign riders make this setup even more efficient.\",\"Print one generic 'Scan for photos and price' rider, link it to a Dynamic QR Code, and repoint that same code to your next listing when the home sells. You reuse the physical rider and skip the cost of reprinting for every new property, so one QR Code on a real estate sign can serve dozens of listings over time.\"]},{\"heading\":\"On printed flyers or open house materials\",\"body\":[\"Flyers and open house sign-in sheets can carry codes that link to photos, pricing, walkthroughs, and full fact sheets. Buyers get everything in one scan, and you reduce the number of printed pages that end up in the recycling bin. A QR Code for real estate flyers also keeps your information centralized, so a single update reaches everyone who scans it. You hand out one sheet and still control what buyers see, even after they leave the open house.\"]},{\"heading\":\"How to create a real estate QR Code\",\"body\":[\"To create a real estate QR Code, choose a destination, generate a Dynamic QR Code, customize it for your brand, download it, and track scans. The whole process takes a few minutes and gives you a code you can update as the listing changes. A real estate QR Code generator like Bitly handles each step in one place, so you don’t need design skills or code to get a print-ready result.\",\"1. Choose your destination (a listing page, virtual tour, Bitly Page, or contact details).\",\"2. Create a Bitly Code.\",\"3. Customize the design with your logo, brand colors, frame, and a call to action (CTA).\",\"4. Download a print-ready file (PNG, JPEG, or SVG) for signs, flyers, or mailers.\",\"5. Track performance in Bitly Analytics and update the destination anytime as the listing changes.\"]}]");
            p0.setCreatedAt(LocalDateTime.parse("Jul 15, 2026 10:00", formatter));
            blogPostRepository.save(p0);
            
            BlogPost p1 = new BlogPost();
            p1.setTitle("How to Shorten Your Spotify Links for More Clicks and Shares");
            p1.setExcerpt("A Spotify link shortener transforms your long, cluttered Spotify URLs into clean, branded short links that earn more clicks and build trust with your audience.");
            p1.setAuthor("Admin");
            p1.setCategory("Social Media, URL Shortening");
            p1.setReadTime("12 min read");
            p1.setImageUrl(urlBase64);
            p1.setContent("[{\"heading\":\"\",\"body\":[\"A Spotify link shortener transforms your long, cluttered Spotify URLs into clean, branded short links that earn more clicks and build trust with your audience. Whether you’re promoting a new single, curating playlists, or growing your listener base, shortened links look professional, fit within character limits, and give you real data on who’s clicking and where.\",\"With 761 million monthly active users as of Q1 2026, Spotify is the world’s largest audio streaming platform. But its default sharing URLs are long strings of random characters that confuse audiences and waste valuable space in your posts, bios, and messages. That disconnect between Spotify’s massive audience and its clunky link format creates a missed opportunity every time you share.\",\"In this guide, you’ll learn why Spotify’s default links hurt your engagement, how to change and customize your Spotify URL with a branded redirect, and how to shorten and track your Spotify links with Bitly. You’ll also discover platform-specific strategies for Instagram, TikTok, X, and email that help you maximize every share.\"]},{\"heading\":\"Key takeaways\",\"body\":[\"Spotify’s default sharing URLs are long strings of random characters that reduce click-through rates and look unprofessional on social platforms.\",\"Bitly transforms Spotify links into branded, memorable short URLs that build trust and encourage greater listener engagement.\",\"You can customize the back-half of your Bitly short link to include your artist name, playlist title, or campaign name for instant context.\",\"Bitly Analytics tracks clicks, geographic data, and referral sources so you can measure which channels drive the most Spotify listens.\",\"Short Spotify links work across Instagram bios, X posts, TikTok profiles, email newsletters, and direct messages without eating up character limits.\"]},{\"heading\":\"Why should you shorten Spotify links?\",\"body\":[\"Spotify’s default URLs create friction with your listeners. They look suspicious, waste character space, and give zero context about where the link leads. Here’s why each of those problems costs you real engagement.\"]},{\"heading\":\"Cluttered appearance\",\"body\":[\"Spotify URLs contain long strings of random characters (like open.spotify.com/playlist/4cOdK2LaU6hj8F7lxA9Nve) that look unprofessional and confusing. They give your audience no context about what they’ll find when they click. When someone sees a URL full of random letters and numbers, they have no reason to trust it.\",\"A branded short link like bit.ly/SummerVibes2026 immediately tells people what to expect. It looks intentional and trustworthy, which matters when you’re trying to increase social media engagement and grow your listener base. The difference between a random string and a descriptive URL can determine whether someone taps or scrolls past.\"]},{\"heading\":\"Less engagement\",\"body\":[\"Long, complicated URLs feel spammy. They erode trust and discourage clicks, especially on mobile, where users are cautious about tapping unfamiliar links. When a URL looks like a jumble of characters, people assume it could lead anywhere, including somewhere unsafe.\",\"This skepticism hits hardest on platforms where attention spans are short. Your followers make split-second decisions about what deserves a tap. A confusing Spotify URL adds just enough doubt to kill that impulse. A short, branded link removes that hesitation entirely by showing exactly what the listener will get.\"]},{\"heading\":\"Difficult to share\",\"body\":[\"Character limits on X (280 characters) and Instagram bios (150 characters) make lengthy Spotify links impractical. They eat into your message space and force awkward formatting that distracts from your actual content. A standard Spotify URL can consume 60 or more characters, leaving you almost no room for context.\",\"With a Spotify link shortener, you reclaim that space for compelling copy, hashtags, or additional context. A short Spotify link also looks cleaner in email signatures, text messages, and anywhere you add a URL on Instagram. You write your message first, then drop in a concise link that doesn’t overwhelm the rest of your post.\"]},{\"heading\":\"How to use shortened Spotify links on Instagram and other platforms\",\"table\":{\"headers\":[\"Platform\",\"Where to place\",\"Why it works\"],\"rows\":[[\"Instagram\",\"Bio link\",\"Fits the 150-character limit and looks professional next to your handle\"],[\"Instagram Stories\",\"Sticker link\",\"Tappable without leaving the app; a branded URL builds trust before the tap\"],[\"X/Twitter\",\"Posts\",\"Saves characters for your message; clean links earn more engagement\"],[\"TikTok\",\"Bio link\",\"Branded short links stand out among generic URLs and signal credibility to new followers\"],[\"Email signatures\",\"Below your name\",\"Adds a low-effort discovery path for contacts every time you send a message\"],[\"Direct messages\",\"In conversation\",\"Short links feel personal and trustworthy in one-on-one messages across any app\"]]},\"body\":[\"Shortened Spotify links work on every platform where you connect with listeners. The key is matching the right link placement to each platform’s format. Here’s a breakdown of where to place your links and why each placement drives results:\",\"Branded short links especially stand out on TikTok, where users scroll fast and make split-second decisions about what to tap. A clean URL like bit.ly/NewTrack2026 catches attention in a way that a 60-character Spotify string never will. TikTok audiences respond to authenticity, and a branded link signals that you care about the details.\"]},{\"heading\":\"How to shorten Spotify links with Bitly\",\"body\":[\"Bitly makes it easy to turn any Spotify URL into a branded, trackable short link in under a minute. Here’s the complete five-step walkthrough to shorten your Spotify link and start tracking performance.\",\"1. Create a Bitly account\",\"2. Copy your Spotify link\",\"3. Shorten with Bitly\",\"4. Share your short link\",\"5. Track performance\"]}]");
            p1.setCreatedAt(LocalDateTime.parse("Jul 09, 2026 10:00", formatter));
